# The SHA-256 of the appimagetool that the Linux packaging step uses.
#
# Format: one "<sha256>  <file name>" line. The packaging script reads the
# first hash in this file, downloads the tool, and refuses to run it unless
# the download hashes to exactly this value. The environment variable
# APPIMAGETOOL_SHA256 overrides this file, for the case where a different
# build of the tool has to be used.
#
# The file name is the asset name of the pinned release, and the release tag
# is in packaging/linux/build.sh next to the download URL. The two have to
# be changed together.
#
# Provenance of the hash below:
#
#   release    AppImage/appimagetool 1.9.1 (2025-11-18), an immutable tag
#   asset      appimagetool-x86_64.AppImage, 15092216 bytes
#   url        https://github.com/AppImage/appimagetool/releases/download/1.9.1/appimagetool-x86_64.AppImage
#   checksum   the sha256 digest GitHub publishes for that release asset, and
#              the value this repository computed from the asset it
#              downloaded and hashed itself.
#
# The tool used to come from the `continuous` release of AppImageKit. That
# tag is a moving one: the bytes under its URL change without notice, so a
# build that fetched it was a build that ran whatever happened to be
# published last, with nothing to compare it against. This pin is what
# replaces that.

ed4ce84f0d9caff66f50bcca6ff6f35aae54ce8135408b3fa33abfc3cb384eb0  appimagetool-x86_64.AppImage
